WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:01.200
♪ (TENSE MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.269
From Boston tonight,
we have a nightmare story

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:05.238
of random crime
and violent death.

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:08.141
SPEAKER: October 23rd, 1989.

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:12.012
A 9-1-1 call comes in
to state police dispatch.

00:00:15.514 --> 00:00:18.118
There's been a murder
at Mission Projects.

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:20.386
(SIRENS WAIL)

00:00:20.486 --> 00:00:22.555
Husband and wife
who was pregnant.

00:00:28.861 --> 00:00:33.465
The Stuart case
is the ultimate truth serum
in the city of Boston.

00:00:34.366 --> 00:00:37.703
Boston was stunned by the murder
of a pregnant woman.

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:40.440
REPORTER: Her husband, Charles,
 was still hospitalized.

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:43.609
SPEAKER 2: When crimes happen
in certain parts of Boston...

00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:45.712
REPORTER 2: And forced his way
 into their car.

00:00:45.779 --> 00:00:47.313
REPORTER 3: They were shot
 by a Black man.

00:00:47.846 --> 00:00:49.782
We all fit the description.

00:00:50.983 --> 00:00:55.421
Cities are naturally segregated.
Boston takes it to an extreme.

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:58.557
Let us go to our neighborhoods
where our kids are safe.

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:01.393
The '70s were a very
tumultuous time in Boston.

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:04.497
SPEAKER 3: There was persistent
 racial violence.

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:07.400
SPEAKER 4: You had heard
 this legend of Boston

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:09.502
as a birthplace of democracy.

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:11.671
But then we also have
another history, as well.

00:01:12.805 --> 00:01:14.574
Send them back to Roxbury.

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:19.546
That people will just call this
the most racist city in America.

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:21.114
(POLICE RADIO CHATTER)

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:22.414
(SIRENS WAILING)

00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:24.684
 SPEAKER 5: I instructed
 the police commissioner

00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:28.288
to be as aggressive
as they ever have been before.

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:30.556
They took my house all apart.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:33.126
SPEAKER 6: They drove me down
 to South Boston.

00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:35.462
I was a-- a scared kid.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.703
"Own free will,"
that's not true.

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:49.776
SPEAKER 7: When you're police,
your job is to investigate
 all aspects.

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:53.145
REPORTER 4: A murder that
grabbed the nation's attention
 takes a bizarre turn.

00:01:53.212 --> 00:01:54.847
This story didn't add up.

00:01:55.514 --> 00:01:58.851
SPEAKER 8: We'd been waiting
for this case to be uncorked.

00:01:59.318 --> 00:02:01.654
SPEAKER 4: When you start
connecting all of these dots,

00:02:01.954 --> 00:02:03.422
it creates a really
ugly puzzle.

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:05.591
SPEAKER 2: We knew what was
 about to happen.

00:02:05.724 --> 00:02:09.495
This is going to end badly
for everybody.

00:02:09.995 --> 00:02:11.631
♪ (TENSE OUTRO MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

